Experiment # 22 : CRUD operations

Node JS – Express application with REST API for CRUD operations over Students data
Aim –
1. Using Express for creating a web application exposing APIs for Creating, Reading,
Updating, Deleting Students data.
2. Familiarize that client side can be native applications expecting data in formats like
json.

Software requirements
•	Node.js
•	npm (Node Package Manager)
•	Notepad++ or visual studio any editor
•	Postman
Procedure
Step 1: Check Node.js installation
Open Command Prompt and execute:
node -v
Check npm:
npm -v

Create a project folder
Open Command Prompt and execute:
cd Desktop
mkdir StudentsCRUD
cd StudentsCRUD

Initialize the Node.js project
npm init -y
This command creates a package.json file to maintain project details and dependencies.

Install Express
npm install express
Express is a Node.js framework used to develop web applications and REST APIs.

Create the JavaScript file
1.	Open Notepad++.
2.	Create a new file.
3.	Type the following program.
4.	Save it as StudentsCRUDapi.js inside the StudentsCRUD folder.

Step 6: Write the Express application

const express = require('express');
const app = express();

app.use(express.json());

// In-memory database
let students = [];
let nextId = 1;

// CREATE - Add a new student
app.post('/students', (req, res) => {
    const { name, age } = req.body;

    if (!name || !age) {
        return res.status(400).json({
            error: 'Name and age are required.'
        });
    }

    const student = {
        id: nextId++,
        name: name,
        age: age
    };

    students.push(student);
    res.status(201).json(student);
});

// READ - Get all students
app.get('/students', (req, res) => {
    res.json(students);
});

// READ - Get student by ID
app.get('/students/:id', (req, res) => {
    const student = students.find(
        s => s.id === parseInt(req.params.id)
    );

    if (!student) {
        return res.status(404).json({
            error: 'Student not found.'
        });
    }

    res.json(student);
});

// UPDATE - Modify student details
app.put('/students/:id', (req, res) => {
    const student = students.find(
        s => s.id === parseInt(req.params.id)
    );

    if (!student) {
        return res.status(404).json({
            error: 'Student not found.'
        });
    }

    const { name, age } = req.body;

    if (name !== undefined) student.name = name;
    if (age !== undefined) student.age = age;

    res.json(student);
});

// DELETE - Remove a student
app.delete('/students/:id', (req, res) => {
    const index = students.findIndex(
        s => s.id === parseInt(req.params.id)
    );

    if (index === -1) {
        return res.status(404).json({
            error: 'Student not found.'
        });
    }

    const removed = students.splice(index, 1);

    res.json({
        message: 'Student deleted.',
        student: removed[0]
    });
});

// Handle invalid routes
app.use((req, res) => {
    res.status(404).json({
        error: 'Route not found.'
    });
});

// Start the server
const PORT = 3002;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(
        `Student CRUD API running at http://localhost:${PORT}`
    );
});

Step 7: Run the application
Open Command Prompt and navigate to the project folder.
cd Desktop\StudentsCRUD
node StudentsCRUDapi.js
Student CRUD API running at http://localhost:3002

 

Step 8: Test the APIs using Postman
Open Postman and create a new HTTP request.
Base URL:
http://localhost:3002
A. CREATE – Insert student details
•	Select method: POST
•	Enter URL: http://localhost:3002/students
•	Select Body → raw → JSON.
•	Enter:
{
  "name": "Rahul",
  "age": 20
}

Click Send.
Expected response:
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Rahul",
  "age": 20
}

TESTING
